From d2810bb1d3769ea0f1db1bed7ef208f80a350b99 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 04:16:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 13/16] Cover flies into Blueprint off the main thread;
 previous follows the coverflow order

- Lyrics -> Blueprint: no view transition. A copy of the cover flies (transform/opacity only) to the record
  label, worked out from the window size (dial/recordGeometry.ts, shared with the dials); Blueprint mounts
  after it lands and fades in around it; the label then shows and the record spins up. The wash joins the
  deferred panels.
- Previous in the immersive view: restarts the song past 3 s, otherwise plays the card just left of the
  playing one; with the shuffle plan the plan steps back (playAt on a history position, pending id so the
  coverflow lays out the step at once). Played cards picked in the coverflow step back the same way.
- Layering: cover-art asks for the view cycle through scene/viewCycleRequest, Blueprint's cover reaches the
  shared holder through page/sharedCover; clear glass goes through the SDK (fb.ui.setBlur) on the injected host.
- The view's backdrop eases between the dark presets and Blueprint.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BozVN1RfiSxLokoA3Q3yHZ
